-- statement:
--   For every prime $q\ne13,19$, including $q=2$, every lift of a rational point through either actual norm map is fixed by valuation inertia. Its continuous Kummer class restricts to zero. Inertia fixes the actual norm kernel and lies in the kernel of its $\mathbf F_{19}$ representation; the normal subgroup generated by all these inertia groups lies in the kernel of the integral representation. All five complete original propositions retain the same chosen Picard scheme, norm maps, actions, topology and valuation inertia. Named downstream consumer: actual character local conditions and Selmer bounds.

